          'Construction glass is used in a wide range of building applications, each requiring specific glass types and properties. Understanding the correct glass for each application helps buyers make informed purchasing decisions.',
          'For windows in residential buildings, clear float glass (4-6 mm) is the basic option. For energy efficiency, insulated glass units (IGUs) with Low-E coatings reduce heat loss and improve comfort. For safety, tempered or laminated glass is used in locations requiring safety glazing (doors, large windows, low-level glazing).',
